Test Name,Summary,Inputs,Steps,Expected Results,Dependencies,Required HW,Required SW,Build Command,Run Command,Source Files,Folder Path
"test_gpio_nedge_random_pads_en","Randomly selects unique GPIO pads (8-39) and configures input + negedge interrupt per pad. Enables group interrupt, toggles SRAM at 0xA0243ffc to generate negedge, waits for IRQ. ISR validates DIN bit, raw and group interrupt status, clears interrupt, and verifies SYSREG raw clear for GPIO0/GPIO1.","GPIO pads 8-39 (rand subset); SRAM 0xA0243ffc; Macros: GPIO0/GPIO1 (select GIC line 87/88)","1) Build with Makefile
2) Enable SYSREG interrupt (GPIO0/1)
3) For i in 0..31 choose unique pad_num randomly
4) Configure MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (pad_num*4) = 0x00140000 (input + negedge)
5) Enable group interrupt bit in MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1
6) Toggle 0xA0243ffc: write ~(1<<pad_num) then 0xFFFFFFFF to create negedge
7) Wait for Default_IRQHandler, validate and clear
8) Repeat for all unique pads
9) finish(test_err)","- DIN[0] reflects expected value during negedge
- Raw status bit set then cleared
- Group interrupt status set for target pad then cleared
- SYSREG RAW_STCR1 cleared (GPIO0/1) successfully
- No errors (test_err == 0)","Headers: lss_sysreg.h, test_common.h; test_define.c arrays; GIC; MIZAR_* register map","Target with MIZAR GPIO block and GIC; access to SRAM addr 0xA0243ffc","C toolchain + environment from $(VERIF)/C_ENV/SOC_ENV/make.include.c_env; console output","make","Load and run on target (env-specific); observe console for SUCCESS/ERROR","program.c; test_define.c; Makefile","TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_nedge_random_pads_en"
"test_gpio_nedge_walking_zeros_pattern","Configures all GPIO pads (8-39) for input + negedge. Enables all group interrupts. Walks a single 0 across bits by writing ~(1<<i) to SRAM 0xA0243ffc to generate negedge per pad. ISR validates DIN, raw and group status, clears interrupts, and checks SYSREG.","GPIO pads 8-39; SRAM 0xA0243ffc; Macros: GPIO0/GPIO1","1) Build with Makefile
2) Enable SYSREG interrupt (GPIO0/1)
3) For i=0..31: set MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4) = 0x00040000 (negedge)
4) Set IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4 = 0x000000FF (input enable)
5) Enable group interrupts: MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 = 0xFFFFFFFF
6) For each i: write 0xFFFFFFFF then ~(1<<i) to 0xA0243ffc to trigger negedge; wait for IRQ and validate; clear
7) finish(test_err)","- DIN[0] matches expected value per pad
- Raw and group interrupt bits asserted then cleared
- SYSREG RAW_STCR1 cleared for GPIO0/1
- No errors (test_err == 0)","Headers: lss_sysreg.h, test_common.h; test_define.c; GIC; MIZAR_* register map","Target with MIZAR GPIO and GIC; SRAM 0xA0243ffc accessible","C toolchain + SOC ENV includes; console","make","Load and run on target; review console output","program.c; test_define.c; Makefile","TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_nedge_walking_zeros_pattern"
"test_gpio_negedge_intr_en","Programs each GPIO pad (8-39) to input + negedge, enables the corresponding group interrupt bit, and toggles SRAM to generate negedge. ISR checks DIN, raw and group status, clears per-pad interrupt register, and verifies SYSREG clear.","GPIO pads 8-39; SRAM 0xA0243ffc; Macros: GPIO0/GPIO1","1) Build with Makefile
2) Enable SYSREG interrupt (GPIO0/1)
3) For i=0..31: addr = MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8 + (i*4); write 0x00140000 (input + negedge)
4) wr_val = 1<<i; enable group bit in MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_INTR1_INTR_EN1 = wr_val
5) Write 0xFFFFFFFF then ~(wr_val) to 0xA0243ffc to trigger negedge; wait for IRQ and validate
6) In ISR: clear per-pad by writing 0x00110001 to GPIO reg; verify group status cleared; clear SYSREG RAW_STCR1 (GPIO0/1)
7) Repeat for all pads; finish(test_err)","- DIN[0] matches pad value during negedge
- Raw and group interrupts asserted then cleared
- SYSREG status cleared
- No errors (test_err == 0)","Headers: lss_sysreg.h, test_common.h; test_define.c; GIC; MIZAR_* register map","Target with MIZAR GPIO and GIC; SRAM 0xA0243ffc accessible","C toolchain + SOC ENV includes; console","make","Load and run on target; review console output","program.c; test_define.c; Makefile","TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_negedge_intr_en"
"test_gpio_op_mode_all_pad_en","Configures GPIO pads (8-39) to output mode and toggles each pad high then low by writing to MIZAR_GPIO_GP0_GPIO_8+(i*4). Reads back pad state via SRAM 0xA0243ffc and validates in check_for_pad_value().","GPIO pads 8-39; SRAM 0xA0243ffc","1) Build with Makefile
2) Set IO_CTRL_GROUP1..4 = 0x00FF00FF (output enable)
3) Enable group interrupts (not strictly required for pad value check)
4) For i=0..31: write 0x00200000 (DOUT=1) then 0x00000000 (DOUT=0) to each pad reg; call check_for_pad_value(i)
5) finish(test_err)","- When DOUT_ONE flag set, corresponding bit in 0xA0243ffc is 1
- When DOUT_ZERO flag set, bit is 0
- No errors (test_err == 0)","Headers: lss_sysreg.h, test_common.h; test_define.c; MIZAR_* register map","Target with MIZAR GPIO block; visibility of pad state via SRAM 0xA0243ffc","C toolchain + SOC ENV includes; console","make","Load and run on target; review console output","program.c; test_define.c; Makefile","TestRepo/gpio/test_gpio_op_mode_all_pad_en"